WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.310
Senators are supposed to be jurors in the
impeachment of a president.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.660
And we learned that yesterday, 21

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:14.559
Republican senators, 21 of the 53 that's nearly
40% of the Republican senators left the Senate

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:20.920
chamber for long periods of time while Adam
Schiff was arguing the case of the prosecution

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.020
during yesterday's day of Donald Trump's Senate
impeachment trial.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.070
Senators are supposed to be in their seats
during the trial.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.610
They're supposed to not miss the proceedings
since this, these proceedings are what they

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.030
will ultimately be using to decide, are we
going to convict or are we going to acquit

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.100
the president of the United States?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:47.739
And yet, 21 Republican senators and two democratic
senators were missing while Adam Schiff was

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:49.340
laying out the case.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.270
They're not even pretending to take this seriously.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.850
And of course, we know they're not taking
it seriously.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:59.219
We know they've already decided that they
will be voting to acquit the president of

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:04.269
the United States, but they could at least
pretend to take it seriously.

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:08.549
Uh, Michael McAuliffe, who's a congressional
reporter, tweeted about this in the middle

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:13.869
of the day yesterday saying quote just counted
21 empty seats on the Republican side of the

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:19.210
Senate, two on the democratic side, a couple
of hours into Adam shifts presentation.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.240
Some are just stretching their legs, but most
are not in the chamber.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.969
Some of them have been out of there for a
while.

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:32.069
They're supposed to decide the fate of Donald
Trump based on the evidence and they are missing

00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:33.069
the evidence.

00:01:33.069 --> 00:01:38.249
And we talked, uh, on yesterday's livestream
of the proceedings about how chief justice

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:43.189
John Roberts, who's presiding over impeachment
as the chief justice of the Supreme court

00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:47.090
does, John Roberts role is procedural.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:50.810
It is not to evaluate the evidence or render
an opinion.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:55.070
Part of the procedure that John Robert is
supposed to be enforcing are the basic rules.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.749
Like senators must be there during the proceedings.

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:04.490
And this actually may be part of why we only
get two camera angles the entire time.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.429
Seaspan has said they've requested to be allowed
to use their cameras in the Senate and to

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.230
control their cameras.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.230
Mitch McConnell does not want that.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:19.010
And when you look at the production of the
uh, stream, uh, unless something's changed

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.790
in the last few hours, there's a shot of the
outside of the Senate, which I believe is

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.599
still a C-SPAN camera.

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:26.819
And then there are two shots.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:28.269
We get two camera angles.

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:33.470
There's like a zoomed in shot of the area
where Schiff and NAD learn the different,

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.150
um, house managers, uh, impeachment managers
stand.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.959
And then there's a slightly wider shot that
lets you see the front of the room.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.880
The tables were Donald Trump's defense attorneys
and the house impeachment managers in John

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:48.099
Roberts are pictured, but no real shots of
the chamber since we would all immediately

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:50.500
realize where the hell are the senators.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.970
This is sick and disgusting.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.050
And, and it is a sham.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.769
Republicans have been saying this is a sham,
the right, it's a sham, but it's a sham because

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:02.959
40% of them are gone for long portions of
Adam's shifts and other presentations.

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:07.450
In a sense, it's almost as if there are 53
empty seats, right?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.189
Because they're all, as far as we know, going
to vote to acquit Donald Trump regardless

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:13.189
of the evidence.

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:17.579
And like I said yesterday on Twitter, how
will they decide whether to convict or acquit

00:03:17.579 --> 00:03:19.780
Trump if they don't see the testimony?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.180
Oh, that's right.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.400
They don't need to.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.040
It's an absolute and total farce.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.909
We're doomed in a sense here.

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:30.870
And this is not even really a matter of partisanship
per se.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.469
It's just childish behavior.

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:35.040
It's immature elected officials.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.950
It's a, uh, with a lot of them.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.349
You know, we keep hearing it.

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:42.250
This is boring and uh, it's, it's boring.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.290
But you are deciding about whether a president
who is only the third president ever to be

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:53.719
impeached is going to become the first president
ever to actually be convicted on impeachment.

00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:54.719
And they're bored.

00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:58.109
They're bored, and they're walking around
while Adam Schiff is presenting evidence.

00:03:58.109 --> 00:03:59.329
It's a truly sorry bunch.

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:04.829
And because of the coverage on Fox news and
elsewhere, which I'm going to talk about momentarily,

00:04:04.829 --> 00:04:10.519
a huge portion of the country will not even
hear that 40% of Republicans were gone during

00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:12.109
much of Adam shift speech.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:18.660
It won't even enter their echo chamber at
all ever, but it reinforces once again for

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.720
better or worse, our voicemail today argues
that this is for worse.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:28.520
Every day of this reinforces that there's
one way to hold Donald Trump accountable.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.060
I don't even have to say it.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.919
We all know what it is and it would be done
in November.

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:33.919
Let me just put it that way.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:35.550
It's nine and a half months away.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.650
He won't be convicted on impeachment.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.910
He's not going to be indicted criminally after
he's out of office.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.530
Yesterday I got questions during our live
stream about how likely do you think it is

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.310
Trump gets indicted when he finally leaves
office?

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.330
I don't think it's likely at all.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.199
I would not take that bet.

00:04:50.199 --> 00:04:55.830
We have one shot to force him to suffer a
consequence and it's by voting him out in

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.830
November.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:06:38.780
Let's now talk about Fox news as coverage.

